1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:02:05,477 --> 00:02:06,777
How many did you eat?

17
00:02:07,987 --> 00:02:09,197
Seventeen.

18
00:02:09,197 --> 00:02:11,367
No, eighteen.

19
00:02:11,367 --> 00:02:13,657
No, maybe nineteen?

20
00:02:13,657 --> 00:02:14,697
And how many are left?

21
00:02:15,287 --> 00:02:16,907
Forget about it.

22
00:02:16,907 --> 00:02:18,327
I need to know.

23
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:20,167
You <i>already</i> know!

24
00:02:20,167 --> 00:02:21,667
Tell me anyway.

25
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:23,497
Eight...

26
00:02:23,497 --> 00:02:24,497
Eight?

27
00:02:24,497 --> 00:02:25,707
Eighty-one!

28
00:02:28,717 --> 00:02:32,167
It'll be fine if I just eat them all, right?

29
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:33,967
Do you think you'll be able to eat all of them?

30
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:35,007
Yes!

31
00:02:35,007 --> 00:02:37,217
I'm Holo, the wise wolf of Yoitz!

32
00:02:37,677 --> 00:02:39,477
You don't need to be so obstinate.

33
00:02:39,477 --> 00:02:41,437
<i>Who's</i> obstinate?

34
00:02:41,437 --> 00:02:42,937
What's the real truth?

35
00:02:42,937 --> 00:02:43,977
It <i>is</i> the real truth.

36
00:02:44,397 --> 00:02:45,687
What's the <i>real</i> real truth?

37
00:02:45,977 --> 00:02:47,397
It's the real real truth!

38
00:02:47,737 --> 00:02:49,857
What's the real, real, real truth?

39
00:02:49,857 --> 00:02:52,317
It's the real, real, real truth!

40
00:02:53,907 --> 00:02:55,947
Actually, I'm getting sick of them.

41
00:02:57,037 --> 00:02:58,077
I'd imagine so.

42
00:02:58,787 --> 00:03:03,207
Even if they're your favorite food, you had twenty yesterday and almost as many today.

43
00:03:04,377 --> 00:03:05,457
But...

44
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:09,257
But I'll show you I can eat them all!

45
00:03:13,547 --> 00:03:15,717
You don't have to be so stubborn about it.

46
00:03:15,717 --> 00:03:19,727
You may be tired of the raw fruit,
but there are lots of other ways to eat apples.

47
00:03:21,687 --> 00:03:24,807
Other ways? What other ways?

48
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:31,727
D-Don't ridicule me!

49
00:03:32,277 --> 00:03:34,567
I've never heard of apples being baked before!

50
00:03:34,987 --> 00:03:38,197
You've seriously never eaten apple pie?

51
00:03:39,157 --> 00:03:41,157
Such a thing really exists?

52
00:03:41,157 --> 00:03:44,117
Yeah, you bake it in a pan with dough.

53
00:03:44,117 --> 00:03:47,417
And if you do that, it becomes chewy...

54
00:03:47,417 --> 00:03:51,457
This isn't a good example,
but it's as if they started rotting.

55
00:03:53,047 --> 00:03:58,007
But just like things taste good right before they go bad, baked apples are extremely tasty, too.

56
00:03:58,007 --> 00:04:01,017
When you eat fresh apples, they moisten your dry throat.

57
00:04:01,017 --> 00:04:03,977
But baked apples are so sweet that they make your throat dry.

58
00:04:06,477 --> 00:04:09,647
But I'm sure you're tired of sweet food.

59
00:04:10,067 --> 00:04:13,777
So, we'll have a change of pace for dinner and have salted meat or fish.

60
00:04:13,777 --> 00:04:14,607
Which would you like?

61
00:04:14,607 --> 00:04:15,407
Meat!

62
00:04:16,697 --> 00:04:19,867
What happened to that girl who looked
like she couldn't eat any more?

63
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:22,407
If it is meat, it's a different story.

64
00:04:23,577 --> 00:04:24,827
Come on!

65
00:04:25,207 --> 00:04:28,287
Hey, don't forget that you need to take care of these apples.

66
00:04:28,287 --> 00:04:29,997
Don't worry.

67
00:04:30,337 --> 00:04:34,217
I have confidence I can eat them all after what I just heard!

68
00:04:34,217 --> 00:04:37,007
Well, I have some business too, so let's go.

69
00:04:37,007 --> 00:04:37,547
Yeah!

70
00:04:45,557 --> 00:04:48,477
I'm treating you to a change in mood so you won't get sick of me.

71
00:04:50,227 --> 00:04:52,357
When I swallow your treats whole, I tend to get heartburn.

72
00:04:52,857 --> 00:04:55,107
Do you want me to tell you that was clever?

73
00:04:55,567 --> 00:04:56,737
I wouldn't mind.

74
00:04:56,737 --> 00:05:01,737
Wolf and the Tail of Happiness

75
00:05:06,237 --> 00:05:08,247
Hmm, well...

76
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:11,497
It's just...

77
00:05:12,417 --> 00:05:13,927
How should I say it? You...

78
00:05:25,017 --> 00:05:28,477
You really do look like a nun.

79
00:05:28,477 --> 00:05:31,567
Indeed. It's convenient for traveling, isn't it?

80
00:05:31,567 --> 00:05:32,267
I suppose.

81
00:05:32,277 --> 00:05:36,127
People are as strange as ever, treating each other so differently

82
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:38,777
based on whether they're wearing a specific piece of cloth or not.

83
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:44,907
There are times when it's convenient
for wolves to wear sheep's clothing too, right?

84
00:05:44,907 --> 00:05:46,117
You're right.

85
00:05:46,117 --> 00:05:50,077
If I wore rabbit's fur, I'm sure you'd fall into my trap instantly.

86
00:05:50,537 --> 00:05:54,957
Then I guess I should carry some apples as protection in case I get caught.

87
00:05:55,417 --> 00:05:58,217
Just when I finally forgot about apples...

88
00:06:01,507 --> 00:06:02,427
But...

89
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:07,977
In your case, looking too much
like a nun could lead to problems.

90
00:06:07,977 --> 00:06:08,887
Like what?

91
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:12,607
Nuns don't drink during the day under any circumstances.

92
00:06:13,567 --> 00:06:15,987
That just makes me an amazing nun, right?

93
00:06:15,987 --> 00:06:18,317
And nuns don't talk like that, either.

94
00:06:19,447 --> 00:06:21,697
I beg your pardon, sir.

95
00:06:23,697 --> 00:06:27,747
In all seriousness, there will be places where dressing as a nun would be a bad idea once we head north.

96
00:06:29,417 --> 00:06:31,037
So what should we do?

97
00:06:31,037 --> 00:06:32,457
So, uh...

98
00:06:33,087 --> 00:06:37,507
Well, it'd make things safer for you
to have a set of clothes like a city girl's.

99
00:06:43,047 --> 00:06:45,807
Let's go and buy some before we eat, then.

100
00:06:45,807 --> 00:06:49,297
If our minds are on business,
our meal won't be as good.

101
00:06:49,607 --> 00:06:52,677
Th-Thank you. I'm glad I don't have to try and persuade you.

102
00:06:53,147 --> 00:06:56,147
Were you thinking I'd say we should eat and drink first?

103
00:06:56,147 --> 00:06:58,857
I won't get distracted by food that easily!

104
00:06:58,857 --> 00:06:59,897
I wonder about that.

105
00:07:01,197 --> 00:07:04,567
I can hardly hamper your attempts to look out for my feelings.

106
00:07:06,327 --> 00:07:11,997
Did you really think I wouldn't notice after you came up with
such a grand, important reason just to buy me some clothes?

107
00:07:13,247 --> 00:07:16,457
Well, I'll cast aside my sheepishness and let you buy them.

108
00:07:16,457 --> 00:07:18,667
It's going to be a cold, cold winter, after all.

109
00:07:19,087 --> 00:07:20,967
Well, you don't have to cast it all aside.

110
00:07:23,297 --> 00:07:25,177
Wh-What's wrong?

111
00:07:25,637 --> 00:07:26,677
I have no money.

112
00:07:28,847 --> 00:07:29,887
You...

113
00:07:31,267 --> 00:07:32,727
That's not what I meant.

114
00:07:33,437 --> 00:07:35,437
I'm saying I don't have small change.

115
00:07:35,437 --> 00:07:37,687
Better too big than too small, as they say.

116
00:07:37,687 --> 00:07:39,397
You can simply use that money, no?

117
00:07:39,697 --> 00:07:43,067
There's also the saying about skinning a rabbit with a meat cleaver.

118
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:46,867
If I used this money at a clothing store,
I can't imagine how annoyed they'd be.

119
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:48,157
I see.

120
00:07:48,157 --> 00:07:51,747
But are gold coins really worth so much?

121
00:07:51,747 --> 00:07:52,827
Of course.

122
00:07:53,287 --> 00:07:58,247
For example, a Lumione gold coin is currently worth thirty-five Trenni silver coins.

123
00:07:58,247 --> 00:08:01,587
If you live humbly, one silver coin can last seven days.

124
00:08:02,677 --> 00:08:04,717
And it's worth thirty-five times that.

125
00:08:04,717 --> 00:08:06,597
That's quite something.

126
00:08:06,597 --> 00:08:07,347
However...

127
00:08:07,717 --> 00:08:10,467
The store said that these clothes were worth two gold coins.

128
00:08:10,467 --> 00:08:15,557
Unlike apples, wouldn't clothes
be something you'd buy with gold coins?

129
00:08:15,557 --> 00:08:19,317
If that were true, most of the people in the city would be naked.

130
00:08:19,317 --> 00:08:24,277
I'm sure the merchant who sold those clothes
must've been quite worried that you'd even pay.

131
00:08:25,107 --> 00:08:27,277
Were these that expensive?

132
00:08:27,277 --> 00:08:28,277
Of course.

133
00:08:28,697 --> 00:08:31,657
So choose some shabby-looking clothes when we buy them.

134
00:08:32,407 --> 00:08:34,917
I'm Holo, the wise wolf of Yoitz!

135
00:08:34,917 --> 00:08:38,087
If I wear something shabby, it'll tarnish my name!

136
00:08:38,087 --> 00:08:42,327
They say that if you are truly beautiful,
then anything should look good on you.

137
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:44,967
I suppose the money exchange is the nextâ€”

138
00:08:44,967 --> 00:08:46,757
Oh, we're going to exchange money?

139
00:08:46,757 --> 00:08:48,957
Then we're going to that bridge, right?

140
00:08:51,017 --> 00:08:52,557
Hey, come on!

141
00:08:52,557 --> 00:08:54,517
Hurry up and walk.

142
00:08:54,517 --> 00:08:56,897
I want to go drinking soon.

143
00:09:01,147 --> 00:09:02,857
Lumione, you say?

144
00:09:02,857 --> 00:09:06,527
Today's market price for it
is thirty-four Trenni silver coins on the dot.

145
00:09:07,237 --> 00:09:08,617
And the handling charge?

146
00:09:08,617 --> 00:09:12,997
Ten Lute coins, or thirty Trie coins.

147
00:09:13,827 --> 00:09:15,497
I'll pay in Lute coins.

148
00:09:16,917 --> 00:09:19,407
Understood. Well then...

149
00:09:19,957 --> 00:09:21,957
Oh, please be careful.

150
00:09:21,957 --> 00:09:25,417
If you drop them, they'll belong to whoever picks them up off the street.

151
00:09:28,007 --> 00:09:28,797
Weiz.

152
00:09:28,797 --> 00:09:29,957
What?

153
00:09:30,467 --> 00:09:32,507
I'm the customer.

154
00:09:33,517 --> 00:09:36,837
Leave the gold coin there. I'm busy right now.

155
00:09:37,227 --> 00:09:40,057
Even though you're not even treating your precious customers properly?

156
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,357
Of course!

157
00:09:41,767 --> 00:09:46,237
It's more important that this precious little lady doesn't drop any coins.

158
00:09:46,237 --> 00:09:47,357
Isn't that right?

159
00:09:47,667 --> 00:09:49,487
My, that makes me happy.

160
00:09:49,487 --> 00:09:51,157
But, dear sir...

161
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:52,697
What is it?

162
00:09:52,697 --> 00:09:56,957
There are just too many coins for my hand to hold.

163
00:09:58,287 --> 00:10:01,707
That's why my hands are there, Holo-san.

164
00:10:01,707 --> 00:10:04,047
My, but we can't do this.

165
00:10:04,047 --> 00:10:07,037
You won't be able to use your precious hands.

166
00:10:07,507 --> 00:10:13,007
Not at all! I'll gladly use my hands so that these coins won't fall from your own.

167
00:10:13,007 --> 00:10:15,557
It does not trouble me in any way.

168
00:10:15,557 --> 00:10:20,307
That is because my chest burns for you with a fire that I cannot bear myself,

169
00:10:20,307 --> 00:10:24,437
and I know that you'll help me bear it in turn!

170
00:10:24,437 --> 00:10:25,357
Weiz!

171
00:10:26,107 --> 00:10:28,277
Did you forget the basics of being a money exchanger?

172
00:10:28,277 --> 00:10:30,487
Silver in a bag, gold in a chest.

173
00:10:30,487 --> 00:10:32,477
Only crude copper coins should be kept in hand!

174
00:10:32,907 --> 00:10:33,817
Geez.

175
00:10:34,577 --> 00:10:38,327
Keeping such a good girl to yourself is an act against God.

176
00:10:38,327 --> 00:10:41,697
Haven't you heard the passage that says to share what bread you can offer?

177
00:10:42,077 --> 00:10:43,287
You want me to share?

178
00:10:44,537 --> 00:10:47,717
There's no lending at the money exchange table.

179
00:10:47,717 --> 00:10:49,377
Only a full exchange or no exchange.

180
00:10:50,547 --> 00:10:54,387
If you take her, the debt she
owes me comes with her,

181
00:10:54,387 --> 00:10:57,217
so you need to show
me you're ready for that.

182
00:10:59,717 --> 00:11:03,267
I can't possibly place a price on you!

183
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:06,477
Just how can you say that, you corrupt merchant!

184
00:11:07,397 --> 00:11:12,567
The scale in my heart is still tilting back and forth right now.

185
00:11:12,567 --> 00:11:17,577
But please, believe that it is not tilting because of the weight of gold coins.

186
00:11:17,577 --> 00:11:20,157
Of course! Of course, I believe you.

187
00:11:21,117 --> 00:11:26,127
You really are a wicked man,
to touch a tilting scale with your hands.

188
00:11:27,757 --> 00:11:28,917
Holo-san...

189
00:11:30,257 --> 00:11:32,007
Come on, let's get going.

190
00:11:32,427 --> 00:11:34,087
H-Hey, Lawrence.

191
00:11:35,217 --> 00:11:39,477
You came to exchange some gold coins,
so are you going shopping or something?

192
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:40,887
That's right.

193
00:11:40,887 --> 00:11:43,597
Prices seem like they're going to rise.

194
00:11:43,597 --> 00:11:44,597
So the faster, the better.

195
00:11:46,197 --> 00:11:47,107
Bye for now.

196
00:11:48,727 --> 00:11:51,767
Do money exchangers work even when the sun sets?

197
00:11:52,147 --> 00:11:57,867
Heaven forbid! You can be sure that money exchangers who use scales after the sun sets are swindlers!

198
00:11:57,867 --> 00:12:00,367
And of course, I'm no swindler.

199
00:12:00,367 --> 00:12:02,037
You heard him.

200
00:12:02,327 --> 00:12:04,997
Once I buy clothes, I'll be going to the tavern early.

201
00:12:04,997 --> 00:12:07,167
You can come if you want when you're done working.

202
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:08,747
Of course, my brother!

203
00:12:08,747 --> 00:12:10,457
It's the usual tavern, right?

204
00:12:11,047 --> 00:12:13,717
It's scary to get drunk in a tavern you don't know.

205
00:12:14,967 --> 00:12:16,097
All right!

206
00:12:16,097 --> 00:12:19,557
Right away! I'll really be there soon!

207
00:12:25,687 --> 00:12:28,017
That was as fun as I thought it'd be.

208
00:12:28,017 --> 00:12:30,817
You'll regret it later if you get him too serious.

209
00:12:31,127 --> 00:12:32,237
Regret it?

210
00:12:32,237 --> 00:12:33,897
He'll follow you around.

211
00:12:33,897 --> 00:12:36,117
You're already following me.

212
00:12:37,067 --> 00:12:40,037
Unlike you, he knows he is playing a game.

213
00:12:40,037 --> 00:12:42,197
It's fun teasing you,

214
00:12:42,197 --> 00:12:44,447
but I want to play with some smart males sometimes.

215
00:12:47,457 --> 00:12:50,207
Both of us know that it's a game,

216
00:12:50,207 --> 00:12:52,507
so could you not act so serious about it?

217
00:12:53,047 --> 00:12:56,007
I'll start blushing, you know.

218
00:12:56,537 --> 00:13:00,847
Well, although that Weiz fellow is more of an eloquent talker than you,

219
00:13:00,847 --> 00:13:06,887
I've lived long enough to know that nothing is so untrustworthy as the words we say.

220
00:13:06,887 --> 00:13:11,937
I'm sure a man of business like yourself would understand that to some degree.

221
00:13:11,937 --> 00:13:16,697
Yeah. I'd tell any lie as long as it brought me profit.

222
00:13:16,697 --> 00:13:18,617
They won't work on me, though.

223
00:13:19,447 --> 00:13:21,947
All right, let's go shopping for clothes.

224
00:13:23,697 --> 00:13:24,497
Hey!

225
00:13:25,997 --> 00:13:29,407
You've twice missed your chance to grasp the happiness God granted.

226
00:13:30,417 --> 00:13:35,337
If you don't grasp it next time,
the tail of happiness might escape you.

227
00:13:35,337 --> 00:13:37,337
Hey, what do you mean?

228
00:13:37,337 --> 00:13:39,967
Hey, Holo! Wait for me!

229
00:13:51,687 --> 00:13:54,517
That one right there is forty Lute.

230
00:13:54,517 --> 00:13:56,737
It's quite durable for that price.

231
00:13:59,527 --> 00:14:05,197
I'm heading north, so could you find some things that'll be cheap and warm for the two of us?

232
00:14:06,537 --> 00:14:07,827
What is your budget?

233
00:14:08,247 --> 00:14:09,917
Two Trenni coins.

234
00:14:09,917 --> 00:14:11,287
Please leave it to me.

235
00:14:11,287 --> 00:14:15,047
A set of robes, two blankets...

236
00:14:15,047 --> 00:14:17,377
And would something like this be fine?

237
00:14:18,757 --> 00:14:20,387
Let's see...

238
00:14:20,387 --> 00:14:22,927
As you can see, I'm a merchant.

239
00:14:22,927 --> 00:14:26,347
On my travels, I became friends with the Milone Company here.

240
00:14:26,637 --> 00:14:28,797
Oh? With Milone?

241
00:14:28,807 --> 00:14:33,397
Right, so I might stop by a few times a year from now on.

242
00:14:33,397 --> 00:14:35,277
Oh, is that so?

243
00:14:35,277 --> 00:14:40,237
Then let me add another blanket along with this robe.

244
00:14:41,117 --> 00:14:43,407
Of course, they've been smoked,

245
00:14:43,407 --> 00:14:45,827
so I guarantee that they'll repel bugs for two years.

246
00:14:59,337 --> 00:15:01,967
Didn't we come to buy clothes for me?

247
00:15:01,967 --> 00:15:03,007
That's right.

248
00:15:04,177 --> 00:15:06,517
Are you telling me to wear that?

249
00:15:07,097 --> 00:15:10,597
Do you want to try and fight the cold off with that robe alone?

250
00:15:12,187 --> 00:15:16,817
If you are upset about my spending your
money without asking, just say so.

251
00:15:16,817 --> 00:15:18,487
I'm Holo, the wise wolf.

252
00:15:18,487 --> 00:15:21,027
I'm smart and I have good business sense, but my nose is sharp too!

253
00:15:21,027 --> 00:15:24,027
The day I wear that, my nose will turn up!

254
00:15:24,617 --> 00:15:29,247
I thought having you suffer a bit
might fix that twisted personality of yours.

255
00:15:31,247 --> 00:15:32,787
Don't get angry.

256
00:15:32,787 --> 00:15:34,337
I'll let you in on the secret later.

257
00:15:35,167 --> 00:15:37,497
Excuse me, sir.

258
00:15:37,877 --> 00:15:38,707
Yes?

259
00:15:38,707 --> 00:15:41,467
Do you have any nice clothes for women?

260
00:15:41,467 --> 00:15:43,217
Clothes for women?

261
00:15:43,217 --> 00:15:45,717
Something that won't cause much trouble in northern cities,

262
00:15:45,717 --> 00:15:47,597
in about her size.

263
00:15:52,897 --> 00:15:55,687
Very well. Please wait just a moment.

264
00:15:56,017 --> 00:15:57,517
How about this?

265
00:15:58,027 --> 00:16:01,057
It's a court attendant's dress that was bought from another shop.

266
00:16:02,907 --> 00:16:04,867
I don't want something that gaudy.

267
00:16:04,867 --> 00:16:07,277
It doesn't suit you?

268
00:16:07,277 --> 00:16:10,617
I want something simpler and easy to change into.

269
00:16:12,757 --> 00:16:14,417
Then...

270
00:16:16,627 --> 00:16:18,627
Sir, how about that?

271
00:16:18,627 --> 00:16:19,337
Excuse me?

272
00:16:20,917 --> 00:16:22,127
I see!

273
00:16:23,967 --> 00:16:26,347
You're quite the person to have laid your eyes on this.

274
00:16:26,717 --> 00:16:30,307
These articles were once worn by a noble.

275
00:16:30,597 --> 00:16:35,267
Just look. The seams are sewn neatly, and it won't tear so easily.

276
00:16:35,767 --> 00:16:38,397
What you should really be looking at is this walnut-colored cap.

277
00:16:38,397 --> 00:16:40,527
Once you wear this over your shoulder

278
00:16:40,527 --> 00:16:46,527
and wear this specially tailored triangular cap just like the servants at this noble's house,

279
00:16:46,527 --> 00:16:50,197
you'll become the most envied girl in town just like that!

280
00:16:52,577 --> 00:16:53,577
A rabbit?

281
00:16:53,907 --> 00:16:55,327
Does it make you hungry?

282
00:16:55,327 --> 00:16:56,537
I like this!

283
00:16:57,537 --> 00:16:58,537
How much is it?

284
00:16:58,537 --> 00:17:00,747
For the two of them, let's see...

285
00:17:01,167 --> 00:17:02,797
Ten Trenni coins.

286
00:17:02,797 --> 00:17:04,877
No, how about nine coins?

287
00:17:06,467 --> 00:17:07,467
Very well.

288
00:17:07,797 --> 00:17:12,427
In deference to the beautiful lady here, I'll make it eight coins.

289
00:17:13,977 --> 00:17:14,847
Well, then...

290
00:17:14,847 --> 00:17:20,727
If someone as cute as myself would show them off for all to see right here and now, would you make it seven coins?

291
00:17:25,147 --> 00:17:28,947
V-Very well, I'll let you have it for seven coins.

292
00:17:28,947 --> 00:17:29,907
Thank you.

293
00:17:30,987 --> 00:17:32,787
Excuse me then.

294
00:17:43,047 --> 00:17:44,337
What do you think?

295
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:46,127
Wonderful!

296
00:17:46,127 --> 00:17:49,297
Paying one Trenni for this was a steal!

297
00:17:53,757 --> 00:17:56,137
Were these clothes too expensive?

298
00:17:56,517 --> 00:17:59,897
No, seven coins for those is quite good.

299
00:18:01,857 --> 00:18:04,027
You still had enough confidence to drive the price down?

300
00:18:04,987 --> 00:18:07,607
I thought if I picked the kind of clothes you are carrying,

301
00:18:07,607 --> 00:18:10,737
we could have purchased them for one
tenth of the price we paid for these.

302
00:18:10,737 --> 00:18:11,827
Yeah.

303
00:18:11,827 --> 00:18:14,827
I actually thought it would've cost more, so don't worry.

304
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:15,447
Okay.

305
00:18:15,867 --> 00:18:18,077
As long as you temper your drinking later,

306
00:18:18,077 --> 00:18:21,287
you'll make up for the seven coins right away.

307
00:18:21,287 --> 00:18:23,127
I don't drink that much!

308
00:18:26,967 --> 00:18:30,837
But still, the way you bargained with him was really cheap.

309
00:18:31,467 --> 00:18:34,637
No matter how expert the
merchant is, he can't beat that.

310
00:18:35,467 --> 00:18:37,597
All males are idiots, after all.

311
00:18:38,937 --> 00:18:41,647
What are you going to do with that?

312
00:18:41,647 --> 00:18:43,767
Taking it with you to the tavern?

313
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:45,567
No, not at all.

314
00:18:45,987 --> 00:18:48,237
But the inn isn't this way.

315
00:18:48,237 --> 00:18:50,447
Yeah, I won't be leaving it at the inn either.

316
00:18:52,527 --> 00:18:54,697
I'm going to sell these at a different clothes shop.

317
00:18:55,117 --> 00:18:58,747
We can buy some clothes for the cold when we head a bit further north.

318
00:18:59,327 --> 00:19:01,327
You're going to sell them?

319
00:19:01,747 --> 00:19:04,207
There's no point in keeping them
if we're not going to use them, right?

320
00:19:05,667 --> 00:19:09,257
That's true, but will they sell high?

321
00:19:09,257 --> 00:19:10,837
I'm not sure.

322
00:19:10,837 --> 00:19:13,047
Seeing a profit would be difficult.

323
00:19:13,047 --> 00:19:14,717
I'll probably have a bit of a loss.

324
00:19:15,177 --> 00:19:17,467
You're still going to sell them if you have a loss?

325
00:19:17,887 --> 00:19:19,177
You don't understand why?

326
00:19:19,177 --> 00:19:21,727
Hold on, I'm thinking now.

327
00:19:29,607 --> 00:19:31,817
Shall I tell you the secret?

328
00:19:32,987 --> 00:19:34,277
I won't ask you to tell me!

329
00:19:34,277 --> 00:19:36,947
But if you want to say it, then go ahead.

330
00:19:38,247 --> 00:19:42,957
That said, it's nothing special,
and you did a better job after all.

331
00:19:43,917 --> 00:19:46,297
This bunch of clothes is worth two coins.

332
00:19:46,297 --> 00:19:50,087
For example, let's say we sell these
at a different store for half the price.

333
00:19:50,087 --> 00:19:51,927
I'd have a loss of one coin.

334
00:19:51,927 --> 00:19:53,007
Right.

335
00:19:53,007 --> 00:19:56,007
But let's direct our attention to something else.

336
00:19:56,557 --> 00:19:58,017
Something else?

337
00:19:58,387 --> 00:19:59,307
That's right.

338
00:19:59,307 --> 00:20:03,267
Anyone can tell at a glance that your robe is high grade, right?

339
00:20:03,267 --> 00:20:04,397
My robe...

340
00:20:04,727 --> 00:20:08,777
It's safe to say that a person wearing it wouldn't ever go to a shop like that.

341
00:20:08,777 --> 00:20:14,367
So that shop owner wanted to have a good relationship with me since I was with you.

342
00:20:14,367 --> 00:20:17,157
Now then, if you were him, what would you do?

343
00:20:17,157 --> 00:20:20,497
I'd sell things cheap to leave a good impression.

344
00:20:20,497 --> 00:20:21,827
That's right.

345
00:20:21,827 --> 00:20:23,707
And what follows from that?

346
00:20:25,417 --> 00:20:28,337
That owner lowered the price on these a bit.

347
00:20:28,337 --> 00:20:31,167
Then he lowered the price on yours a lot.

348
00:20:31,587 --> 00:20:36,347
We were the customers who'd taken two coins worth of these ragged clothes off his hands after all.

349
00:20:36,347 --> 00:20:40,537
However, there's a huge gap between the two prices.

350
00:20:40,537 --> 00:20:42,597
And what does that mean?

351
00:20:42,977 --> 00:20:46,607
If we think about the total balance, we saved a lot.

352
00:20:46,607 --> 00:20:48,147
Well done.

353
00:20:52,147 --> 00:20:54,737
What a cheap trick. A completely cheap trick!

354
00:20:56,027 --> 00:20:57,367
That trick?

355
00:20:57,367 --> 00:20:58,327
Fool!

356
00:20:58,327 --> 00:21:01,747
I'm amazed you even thought of that.

357
00:21:01,747 --> 00:21:03,827
That's called business sense.

358
00:21:04,247 --> 00:21:08,037
Though your brute force technique was better in the end.

359
00:21:08,037 --> 00:21:09,287
Naturally.

360
00:21:09,627 --> 00:21:13,087
Your shallow thinking can't beat my scheming.

361
00:21:13,087 --> 00:21:14,257
You've said it now.

362
00:21:15,257 --> 00:21:16,207
You think you can win?

363
00:21:16,757 --> 00:21:18,847
Well, if you're confident about it,

364
00:21:18,847 --> 00:21:22,177
maybe you could show me your skills when we go drinking.

365
00:21:22,177 --> 00:21:23,597
When we go drinking?

366
00:21:25,767 --> 00:21:28,437
Make sure you pay a high price for me, now.

367
00:21:28,437 --> 00:21:29,817
Oh, I'll buy you, all right.

368
00:21:29,817 --> 00:21:31,597
But the payment will be in apples.

369
00:21:32,187 --> 00:21:34,487
You're pretty tough, too.

370
00:21:34,987 --> 00:21:37,277
If you bake me, I might become a bit sweeter.

371
00:21:38,527 --> 00:21:40,407
You're pretty well baked already.

372
00:21:40,737 --> 00:21:43,407
Males baked with jealousy are too sweet to eat.

373
00:21:43,907 --> 00:21:45,497
What about you, then?

374
00:21:45,497 --> 00:21:47,497
Do you want to have a bite and see for yourself?

375
00:21:51,167 --> 00:21:52,707
I'll think about it.

376
00:22:03,387 --> 00:22:06,557
You grasped it properly the third time.

377
00:23:40,497 --> 00:23:45,007
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Proper Balance."</i>

378
00:23:45,827 --> 00:23:49,997
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Proper Balance."</i>

